**Given:-** sin 18° = {sqrt 5 - 1} over {4}

**To find:- ** cosec 18°

**Formula used:-** cosec theta = {1over sintheta} 

**Calculation:-** By using the relation between sin theta and cosec theta,

⇒cosec 18° = {1over sin 18circ} 

Substituting the value of sin 18° by {sqrt 5 - 1} over {4},

⇒cosec 18° = {1 over frac{sqrt{5}-1}{4} }

⇒cosec 18° = {4 over sqrt{5}-1}

Rationalising the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator by sqrt{5}+1

⇒cosec 18° = {4 times ({sqrt{5}+1})over ( sqrt{5}+1) times ({sqrt{5}-1})}

By using the formula **(a - b) × (a + b) = a² - b²** 

⇒cosec 18° = {4 times ({sqrt{5}+1})over ( sqrt{5})²-{(1)}² }

⇒cosec 18° = {4 times ({sqrt{5}+1})over4 }

⇒cosec 18° = sqrt{5}+1

**The value of **cosec 18° ** is sqrt{5}+1**
